-- allium: 3
-- scheduling.allium
--
-- Shared scheduling types and host-side periodic scheduling support.
--
-- Scope: Schedule value type and ScheduleType enum (shared across any spec that
--        needs a structured schedule); host-side periodic scheduling for background
--        jobs that run independently of any agent session (Zotero sync, RSS feeds).
-- Includes: Schedule (value), ScheduleType (enum), compute_next_check concept.
-- Excludes:
--   - Per-session agent-initiated tasks — fully specced in agent-to-agent.allium
--     (ScheduledTask entity, schedule_task / cancel_task / pause_task /
--     resume_task / update_task rules, ScheduledTaskRecurrenceCloned).
--   - Inbound message recurrence — sessions.allium (InboundMessage.recurrence,
--     process_after, InboundRecurrenceCloned).
--   - Zotero sync details — zotero.allium.
--
-- Relationship to agent-to-agent.allium:
--   agent-to-agent.allium covers agent-initiated scheduling via the schedule_task
--   MCP tool. It uses raw cron strings and Timestamps directly on ScheduledTask
--   rather than the Schedule value type here. This spec covers the host-side
--   background scheduling layer that fires without an agent session driving it.
--
-- Status: skeleton. Schedule and ScheduleType are defined and ready for use by
--   zotero.allium. The host-periodic scheduling entity and rules are stubs —
--   implement them here when the first concrete consumer (Zotero or RSS) is wired up.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A structured schedule specification for host-side periodic features.
-- Carries the schedule type alongside its value so callers can branch on
-- cron vs interval vs once without parsing the value string.
--
-- Agent-initiated tasks in agent-to-agent.allium use raw strings directly
-- on ScheduledTask.recurrence / process_after and do not use this type.
-- allium-ignore allium.definition.unused
value Schedule {
    type: ScheduleType
    value: String           -- cron expr ("0 9 * * 1-5"), interval ms ("3600000"),
                            -- or ISO timestamp ("2026-01-01T09:00:00Z") for once
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum ScheduleType { cron | interval | once }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Stubs: Host-side Periodic Scheduling
------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- The items below are planned for this spec and are referenced by zotero.allium.
-- Implement here once a concrete host-periodic consumer is wired up.
--
-- compute_next_check(schedule, from) — helper used by zotero.allium rules.
--   Advances from `from`, not from `now`, so the schedule stays regular even
--   when a check runs late. Missed intervals are skipped forward to the next
--   future slot rather than fired back-to-back. Cron mode resolves timezone
--   using the same priority order as agent-to-agent.allium
--   ScheduledTaskRecurrenceCloned: TZ env var → .env TZ → system locale → UTC.
--   Once mode returns null after the first firing (consumed; does not repeat).
--
-- Recovery on restart — when the host starts up and a periodic job has a
--   next_check in the past, it is advanced to the next future slot rather than
--   fired immediately. This prevents a burst of back-to-back runs after a long
--   outage.
